WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.164
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:08.735
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:13.626
Unit eight: Sportsmanship. Today you will use 'even though' and 'no matter what'.

4
00:00:13.926 --> 00:00:16.532
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.711
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:22.609
Fair play.

7
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:26.324
Fair play means playing honestly and by the rules.

8
00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:29.032
The team won a prize for fair play.

9
00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:32.362
Your turn. Say: Fair play.

10
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.294
Fair play.

11
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.132
Integrity.

12
00:00:39.117 --> 00:00:42.591
Integrity means being honest even when no one is watching.

13
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:45.647
She showed integrity and admitted the foul.

14
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.751
Your turn. Say: Integrity.

15
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.822
Integrity.

16
00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:55.049
Respect opponents.

17
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.653
Respect opponents means to treat the other team well.

18
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.493
We shake hands to respect opponents.

19
00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:05.293
Your turn. Say: Respect opponents.

20
00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.552
Respect opponents.

21
00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:11.759
Graceful loser.

22
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.551
Graceful loser means someone who loses politely.

23
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.811
Be a graceful loser and congratulate the winner.

24
00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:22.603
Your turn. Say: Graceful loser.

25
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.106
Graceful loser.

26
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.014
Humble winner.

27
00:01:30.017 --> 00:01:33.050
Humble winner means someone who wins without showing off.

28
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.731
A humble winner thanks the other team.

29
00:01:36.317 --> 00:01:38.969
Your turn. Say: Humble winner.

30
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:42.927
Humble winner.

31
00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:44.592
Ethics.

32
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:48.070
Ethics means rules about right and wrong.

33
00:01:48.683 --> 00:01:50.996
Cheating goes against sports ethics.

34
00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:53.818
Your turn. Say: Ethics.

35
00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:57.726
Ethics.

36
00:01:58.483 --> 00:01:59.775
Code of conduct.

37
00:02:00.783 --> 00:02:03.491
Code of conduct means rules on how to behave.

38
00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:06.385
Every player signs the code of conduct.

39
00:02:06.983 --> 00:02:09.903
Your turn. Say: Code of conduct.

40
00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.081
Code of conduct.

41
00:02:14.817 --> 00:02:15.748
Referee.

42
00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.493
Referee means the official who controls a game.

43
00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:21.874
Never shout at the referee.

44
00:02:22.483 --> 00:02:24.799
Your turn. Say: Referee.

45
00:02:27.633 --> 00:02:28.751
Referee.

46
00:02:29.517 --> 00:02:30.402
Discipline.

47
00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:34.682
Discipline means controlling your behaviour and training hard.

48
00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:37.562
Discipline helps athletes stay calm.

49
00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.907
Your turn. Say: Discipline.

50
00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:44.756
Discipline.

51
00:02:45.517 --> 00:02:46.669
Team spirit.

52
00:02:47.683 --> 00:02:51.134
Team spirit means a feeling of loyalty and support in a team.

53
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.680
Our team spirit is amazing.

54
00:02:54.283 --> 00:02:57.005
Your turn. Say: Team spirit.

55
00:02:59.867 --> 00:03:00.972
Team spirit.

56
00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:02.451
Honor.

57
00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.680
Honor means great respect earned by doing what is right.

58
00:03:07.283 --> 00:03:09.399
It is an honor to play for my school.

59
00:03:09.983 --> 00:03:12.334
Your turn. Say: Honor.

60
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.143
Honor.

61
00:03:16.883 --> 00:03:18.349
Sporting behavior.

62
00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.708
Sporting behavior means fair and polite actions in sport.

63
00:03:23.317 --> 00:03:25.757
The coach praised our sporting behavior.

64
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.828
Your turn. Say: Sporting behavior.

65
00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:33.109
Sporting behavior.

66
00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.748
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:38.583 --> 00:03:42.153
Visal, I heard your team lost the final. How do you feel?

68
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:48.538
Even though we lost, we stayed respectful. We shook hands with everyone.

69
00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:52.894
That's a graceful loser. Did the referee make a mistake?

70
00:03:53.983 --> 00:03:58.328
Maybe, but no matter what happens, we respect the referee.

71
00:03:59.417 --> 00:04:01.950
Why is sportsmanship more important than winning?

72
00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:07.917
Because winning lasts one day, but integrity and honor last forever.

73
00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:10.602
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.703
Grammar focus: even though and no matter what.

75
00:04:15.003 --> 00:04:16.097
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:16.783 --> 00:04:19.270
Even though we lost, we stayed respectful.

77
00:04:20.183 --> 00:04:22.427
No matter what happens, play fair.

78
00:04:23.317 --> 00:04:26.036
No matter what the score is, respect your opponents.

79
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.789
'Even though' introduces a surprising fact. 'No matter what' means 'in every situation'.

80
00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.851
Be careful! Don't say: No matter happens, play fair.

81
00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.392
Say: No matter what happens, play fair.

82
00:04:41.692 --> 00:04:43.703
Say 'no matter what', not 'no matter'.

83
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.280
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:49.207
More Than a Game.

85
00:04:49.507 --> 00:04:52.737
Fair play and integrity define good sportsmanship.

86
00:04:53.733 --> 00:04:57.045
Even though our team lost the final, we stayed respectful.

87
00:04:58.033 --> 00:05:00.114
We shook hands and thanked the referee.

88
00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:05.073
No matter what happens, a humble winner and a graceful loser show honor.

89
00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.542
Respecting opponents matters more than winning.

90
00:05:09.633 --> 00:05:13.473
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:14.317 --> 00:05:16.525
blank we lost, we stayed respectful.

92
00:05:16.825 --> 00:05:20.502
A, Even though. B, Because. C, So.

93
00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:25.904
The answer is A: Even though.

94
00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.468
The official who controls a game is the blank.

95
00:05:29.768 --> 00:05:33.270
A, referee. B, opponent. C, coach.

96
00:05:36.833 --> 00:05:38.914
The answer is A: referee.

97
00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.909
Being honest even when no one is watching is blank.

98
00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:47.512
A, integrity. B, discipline. C, team spirit.

99
00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:52.950
The answer is A: integrity.

100
00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:57.330
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:58.183 --> 00:06:01.077
Why is sportsmanship important, even more than winning?

102
00:06:09.883 --> 00:06:11.279
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:11.579 --> 00:06:23.125
Sportsmanship is important because it shows respect. Even though winning feels great, no matter what happens, we should play fair and respect our opponents.

104
00:06:23.425 --> 00:06:25.250
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:30.544
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and even though and no matter what.

106
00:06:30.844 --> 00:06:35.540
Today's value is sportsmanship. Play fair and shake hands, win or lose.

107
00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:38.260
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

108
00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:40.759
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

